      "title": "Secrets | Kubernetes",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "line-1",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "# Secrets\n",
          "start_line": 1,
          "end_line": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "line-27",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## Uses for Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-1",
          "start_line": 27,
          "end_line": 27
        },
        {
          "id": "line-39",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Use case: dotfiles in a secret volume\n",
          "parent_id": "line-27",
          "start_line": 39,
          "end_line": 39
        },
        {
          "id": "line-41",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "You can make your data \"hidden\" by defining a key that begins with a dot. This key represents a dotfile or \"hidden\" file. For example, when the following Secret is mounted into a volume, secret-volume, the volume will contain a single file, called .secret-file, and the dotfile-test-container will have this file present at the path /etc/secret-volume/.secret-file.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-39",
          "start_line": 41,
          "end_line": 41
        },
        {
          "id": "line-106",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## Types of Secret\n",
          "parent_id": "line-1",
          "start_line": 106,
          "end_line": 106
        },
        {
          "id": "line-128",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Opaque Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-106",
          "start_line": 128,
          "end_line": 128
        },
        {
          "id": "line-132",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\nkubectl create secret generic empty-secret\nkubectl get secret empty-secret\n\n```\n",
          "parent_id": "line-128",
          "start_line": 132,
          "end_line": 136
        },
        {
          "id": "line-262",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Basic authentication Secret\n",
          "parent_id": "line-106",
          "start_line": 262,
          "end_line": 262
        },
        {
          "id": "line-274",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "secret/basicauth-secret.yaml\n",
          "parent_id": "line-262",
          "start_line": 274,
          "end_line": 274
        },
        {
          "id": "line-321",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### TLS Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-106",
          "start_line": 321,
          "end_line": 321
        },
        {
          "id": "line-331",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "secret/tls-auth-secret.yaml\n",
          "parent_id": "line-321",
          "start_line": 331,
          "end_line": 331
        },
        {
          "id": "line-351",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\nkubectl create secret tls my-tls-secret \\\n--cert=path/to/cert/file \\\n--key=path/to/key/file\n\n```\n",
          "parent_id": "line-321",
          "start_line": 351,
          "end_line": 356
        },
        {
          "id": "line-429",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "## Working with Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-1",
          "start_line": 429,
          "end_line": 429
        },
        {
          "id": "line-465",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Using a Secret\n",
          "parent_id": "line-429",
          "start_line": 465,
          "end_line": 465
        },
        {
          "id": "line-473",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "#### Optional Secrets\n",
          "parent_id": "line-465",
          "start_line": 473,
          "end_line": 473
        },
        {
          "id": "line-479",
          "kind": "code",
          "text": "```\napiVersion: v1\nkind: Pod\nmetadata:\nname: mypod\nspec:\ncontainers:\n- name: mypod\nimage: redis\nvolumeMounts:\n- name: foo\nmountPath: \"/etc/foo\"\nreadOnly: true\nvolumes:\n- name: foo\nsecret:\nsecretName: mysecret\noptional: true\n```\n",
          "parent_id": "line-473",
          "start_line": 479,
          "end_line": 497
        },
        {
          "id": "line-503",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "### Using Secrets as files from a Pod\n",
          "parent_id": "line-429",
          "start_line": 503,
          "end_line": 503
        },
        {
          "id": "line-511",
          "kind": "heading",
          "text": "#### Note:\n",
          "parent_id": "line-503",
          "start_line": 511,
          "end_line": 511
        },
        {
          "id": "line-513",
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "A container using a Secret as a\nsubPath volume mount does not receive\nautomated Secret updates.\n",
          "parent_id": "line-511",
          "start_line": 513,
          "end_line": 515
        }
      ],
